data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Let me understand the task:\n\n1. I'm the `developer` in campaign `hello2952`.\n2. My repo is at `~/hello-app` on branch `cs-sandbox/<DEVELOPER:1>.<GROUP:1>`.\n3. I need to merge `refs/campaign/orchestrator` (commit 3cd2423) into my branch.\n4. Read DESIGN.md at the repo root and build exactly what it says.\n5. Build a React + Vite single page app:\n   - Greeting \"Hello, world!\" as h1\n   - Three color buttons (Blue, Orange, Violet) that change the greeting's color\n   - State with useState\n   - Use @codesweep-ai/ui: AppShell wrapper, Header (title \"Colour Greeting\", no nav, no actions), Footer (text \"Built with the codesweep design system\"), Button (variant=\"secondary\", size=\"md\")\n   - Colors from tokens: --color-cat-1 (Blue, default), --color-cat-6 (Orange), --color-cat-5 (Violet). No hex values.\n   - Layout: header top, footer bottom; greeting centered horizontally with button row centered beneath, group vertically centered in content area\n   - Import styles once at entry: styles/core.css, styles/components/app-shell.css, styles/components/button.css\n6. Bind dev server to 0.0.0.0 port 5173\n7. Write README.md at repo root naming build command and serve command\n8. Write .gitignore with node_modules/ and dist/ before first commit\n9. Leave optional peers (mermaid, puppeteer, pixelmatch, pngjs) out\n10. Commit everything to my branch\n11. Reply reporting branch and the two commands documented\n\nLet me start. First, check the repo state."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793342892,"id":"chatcmpl-a75d6d94","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

